    {
      "id": "399c4a55-2675-4bed-aff8-0286ca36cfe0",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#E1D7B2",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## YouTube Publishing Monitor - Sheets + Slack\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule to monitor a YouTube channel’s videos, retrieve recent video data, and identify items around a 30-minute timing window. It branches by video/publishing status, compares current status against rows in Google Sheets, updates the sheet when a change is detected, and sends Slack notifications for relevant updates. No-op nodes terminate paths where the stored status already matches or no action is needed.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger with the desired polling interval.\n- Set up YouTube Data API access in the HTTP Request nodes, including the API key or credential, channel ID, playlist ID, and any query parameters used to retrieve videos.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and use a tracking sheet with **Video ID** and **Status** columns. Recent private/public videos use Append or Update with **Video ID** as the matching key.\n- Connect Slack credentials and choose the target channel or user for each Slack message node.\n- Confirm the status values and timing conditions used by the IF and Switch nodes match the publishing states you want to monitor.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the schedule frequency, the “30 minutes ago” timing window, the YouTube status routing rules, the Google Sheets columns being compared or updated, and the Slack message text/channel for each notification path."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1c4d5ea9-39bd-48dd-baf0-07383f606ced",
